  "articleBody": "Even if you don't see water dripping inside your Alliance home after a storm, that doesn't mean your roof is out of the woods. Texas storms, especially those with high winds or hail, can leave behind damage that's easy to miss from the ground but can compromise your roof's integrity over time. Getting a post-storm inspection is a smart move, and knowing what to look for can help you decide when it's time to call in the pros. We're here to help you understand the subtle cues your roof might be giving you.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\n\n- [ ] Granule loss from shingles — Look for dark spots on your asphalt shingles or an accumulation of shingle granules in your gutters. This indicates hail impact has worn away the protective top layer, reducing your roof's lifespan.\n- [ ] Dented or damaged gutters and downspouts — Hail or falling debris can dent or dislodge gutters. If your gutters aren't channeling water away properly, it can lead to fascia and foundation issues.\n- [ ] Missing, cracked, or curled shingles — Strong winds can lift and tear shingles, or even remove them entirely. Cracked or curled shingles can also be a sign of underlying damage or age accelerated by weather.\n- [ ] Damage to other exterior elements — Check your fences, siding, outdoor units, and even your car for dents or signs of impact. If these are damaged, it's a strong indicator that your roof likely took a hit too.\n- [ ] Water stains on ceilings or walls — This is a more obvious sign of a leak, but it might take time to appear. If you see new discoloration, it’s a clear signal that water is getting in where it shouldn't.\n- [ ] Lifted or bent flashing around chimneys or vents — Flashing protects vulnerable areas where your roof meets other structures. If it's lifted, bent, or otherwise compromised, water can easily seep underneath, leading to leaks.\n- [ ] Debris on your roof or in your yard — Large branches or other storm debris on your roof could have caused direct impact damage, even if you can't see the specific spot from the ground.\n\nHow to use this checklist: Go through these points from a safe vantage point, like your yard. If you notice any of these signs after a storm, it’s definitely time to get a professional post-storm roof inspection. Don't wait for a small problem to become a major repair. Contact Discounted Roofing Co. to schedule a comprehensive inspection and get peace of mind.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}